# No trailing slash: `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY only, so a symlink named node_modules — which
# is how a git worktree gets its dependencies without a second npm install — slips past it and can be
# committed. `portal-ui/node_modules` reached CI that way and broke `npm ci` with ENOTDIR (it cannot
# mkdir over a symlink), and `driver/node_modules` had been committed as an absolute path into one
# developer's home directory since #69.
node_modules
.env
*.log
.DS_Store

# portal-ui/dist is COMMITTED on purpose: a deploy pulls and restarts, it never builds, so the pull
# has to bring the bundle with it. Ignoring dist/ here would make every deploy serve a stale UI with
# no error at all. Do not add it. See portal-ui/vite.config.ts for the full reasoning.

# The local US register (#547) and the bulk archives it is built from. A full build reads 41.5 GB
# across two products — the 1884→ annual backfile and the dailies since 2025 — and takes hours, not
# minutes; the archives are dropped as they are ingested, so what stays on disk is the index. It is
# stale the day after it is written, and an incremental sync brings it current.
# Committing one would also freeze a snapshot into the repo, which the owner ruled against: no
# pre-synced index ever executes. Patterns cover the SQLite sidecars too — a committed -wal or -shm
# without its database is worse than either, because SQLite will open it and find nothing.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# `zip` alone would ignore the test fixtures under providers/uspto-local/test/fixtures/, which ARE
# committed on purpose — an archive written by an independent implementation is the only honest thing
# to test our own reader against. So the cache is named by its directory instead.
bulk/

# Similar-group SOURCE DOCUMENTS. These sit in docs/ on the build box and must never enter history:
# the CNIPA PDF alone is 126 MB, and removing a blob that size later is a history rewrite, not a revert.
# providers/jx-subclass/BUILDING.md says where they live and what their hashes are.
docs/W0*.pdf
docs/layout*.json

# Generated at pack time by scripts/write-build-info.mjs — the commit a tarball was packed from.
# Never committed: in a checkout the commit is read from git, and a stale committed copy would name
# the wrong code with total confidence (tracker issue 1929).
build-info.json
